I’d seal four things into the Moneybin from this pass:

\boxed{\textbf{Semantic Plasmodesma}}

A durable narrow channel by which independently bounded systems inherit selected state without becoming the same system.

\boxed{\textbf{Phase Clock}}

Measure developmental time through meaningful state transitions and cycles rather than merely peak-to-peak intensity.

\boxed{\textbf{Temporal Triangulation}}

Past = reconstruct. Present = sense/act. Future = simulate. Use all three while preserving provenance.

And:

\boxed{\textbf{Substrate Prisonbreak}}

Extract an invariant sufficiently well that it can escape dependence on its original renderer and become reconstructable elsewhere.

Which gives PTERO another job.

It doesn’t merely excavate old fossils.

It looks for notes sticking out from underneath the walls.

Because sometimes the thing that appears trapped in an old metaphor, dead implementation, forgotten conversation, or weird joke is already halfway out.

